UID:35331-1790089200-1790269200@philosophy.utoronto.ca
SUMMARY:2026 Jerome S. Simon Memorial Lectures (Barbara Vetter\, Freie Universität Berlin)
DESCRIPTION:We are pleased to announce Barbara Vetter as our esteemed speaker for the 2026 Jerome S. Simon Memorial Lectures. Dr. Vetter is a professor of theoretical philosophy at Freie Universität Berlin\, and co-director of the “Human Abilities” project (www.human-abilities.de). Her work focuses on the metaphysics and epistemology of modal properties — dispositions\, abilities\, and so on — and their role in the metaphysics and epistemology of modality. She published Potentiality: From Dispositions to Modality with the Oxford University Press in 2015. In 2026\, she received a Gottfried Wilhelm Leibniz prize.  Dr. Vetter is currently working on a book that develops an agency-based approach to the epistemology of modality. \nMore information on the three lectures to follow.
URL:https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/event/2026-jerome-s-simon-memorial-lectures-barbara-vetter-freie-universitat-berlin/
LOCATION:Jackman Humanities Building 100
CATEGORIES:Alumni,Graduate,St. George
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/wp-content/uploads/Philosophisches-Symposium-Potentialitaet_2019-03-18-_537_-ORG-cropped.jpg
END:VEVENT
